As a [[Premier League]] team, Chelsea entered the competition in the third round where they played at home at [[Stamford Bridge (stadium)|Stamford Bridge]] against [[EFL League Two|League Two]] side [[Morecambe F.C.|Morecambe]], whom had been affected by a [[COVID-19]] outbreak at the club prior to the match.<ref>{{cite web |first=James |last=Robson |url=https://www.standard.co.uk/sport/football/chelsea-fc-news-fa-cup-morecambe-covid-coronavirus-outbreak-b695490.html |title=Chelsea's FA Cup tie against Morecambe expected to get go-ahead after Covid outbreak |work=[[Evening Standard]] |date=5 January 2021 |access-date=24 January 2021}}</ref>  [[Mason Mount]] opened the scoring in the 18th minute with a {{convert|25|yd|adj=on}} strike before [[Timo Werner]] made it 2–0 to Chelsea before half-time from close range.  [[Callum Hudson-Odoi]] scored four minutes after the interval and [[Kai Havertz]] made it 4–0 after [[Header (association football)|heading]] in a [[Cross (association football)|cross]] from [[César Azpilicueta]].<ref>{{cite web|title=Werner scores as Chelsea see off Morecambe|publisher=[[BBC Sport]]|date=8 January 2021|url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/55575484|access-date=17 April 2021| first= Neil | last= Johnston | archive-date=24 January 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210124041423/https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/55575484|url-status=live}}</ref> In the fourth round, they played [[EFL Championship|Championship]] side [[Luton Town F.C.|Luton Town]] at home.  Chelsea were 2–0 ahead inside 17 minutes with two goals from [[Tammy Abraham]].  [[Jordan Clark (English footballer)|Jordan Clark]] reduced the deficit, scoring after an error from [[Kepa Arrizabalaga]], but Abraham completed his [[Hat-trick (association football)|hat-trick]] in the 74th minute.  Werner missed a late [[Penalty kick (association football)|penalty]] and the match ended 3–1 to Chelsea.<ref>{{cite web|title=Abraham hat-trick sees off Luton| first= Jess | last = Anderson | publisher=[[BBC Sport]]|date=22 January 2021|url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/55770051|access-date=17 April 2021|archive-date=25 February 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210225234912/https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/55770051|url-status=live}}</ref> 

Their opposition for the fifth round was Championship team [[Barnsley F.C.|Barnsley]] who they played away at [[Oakwell]].  After a goalless first half, Abraham gave Chelsea the lead midway through the second, with his side's only shot on target in the match. A late shot from [[Michael Sollbauer]] was cleared off the goalline by Abraham, and Chelsea progressed to the quarter-final with a 1–0 victory.<ref>{{cite web|title=Chelsea beat Barnsley to set up Sheff Utd tie|publisher=[[BBC Sport]]| first= Neil | last= Johnston | date=10 February 2021| url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/55955768| access-date=17 April 2021| archive-date=21 February 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210221222359/https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/55955768|url-status=live}}</ref> There they played fellow Premier League side [[Sheffield United F.C.|Sheffield United]] at Stamford Bridge.  Midway through the first half, Chelsea took the lead when [[Oliver Norwood]] deflected [[Ben Chilwell]]'s cross into the Sheffield United net for an [[own goal]].  In second-half [[stoppage time]], Chelsea counter-attacked as Sheffield United pushed players up the field, and [[Hakim Ziyech]]'s 92nd minute strike secured a 2–0 win.<ref>{{cite web|title=Chelsea move into FA Cup semi-finals|publisher=[[BBC Sport]]|date=19 March 2021|url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/56415023| first = Michael | last= Emons| access-date=17 April 2017|archive-date=19 March 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210319141154/https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/56415023|url-status=live}}</ref> Chelsea then faced the Premier League leaders Manchester City in the semi-final at Wembley Stadium which was being used as a neutral venue.  The first half ended goalless and ten minutes into the second half, Ziyech scored from Werner's pass. 
No further goals were scored and Chelsea reached their fourth final in five years with a 1–0 victory.<ref>{{cite web|title=Thomas Tuchel's side advance to FA Cup final to end City's quadruple hopes|publisher=[[BBC Sport]]|date=17 April 2021| first= Phil | last = McNulty |authorlink = Phil McNulty | url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/56725442|access-date=17 April 2021|archive-date=17 April 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210417082002/https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/56725442|url-status=live}}</ref>

