==Post-match==
[[File:Brendan Rodgers 2014 (cropped).jpg|thumb|upright|alt=Brendan Rodgers|Brendan Rodgers ''(pictured in 2014)'' won his seventh final as a manager.]]

As President of The Football Association, Prince William, Duke of Cambridge, presented the FA Cup to Schmeichel, Leicester City's [[Captain (association football)|captain]]. Due to the [[COVID-19 pandemic in England]], the presentation took place on the pitch instead of in the Royal Box. Players and managers of both clubs picked up their own medals.<ref>{{Cite web|last=Coke|first=Hope|title=The Duke of Cambridge to champion the return of spectator sports at FA Cup final|url=https://www.tatler.com/article/prince-william-will-attend-fa-cup-final|access-date=15 May 2021|work=[[Tatler]]|date=11 May 2021 |archive-date=15 May 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210515105601/https://www.tatler.com/article/prince-william-will-attend-fa-cup-final|url-status=live}}</ref> The FA did not punish Leicester players Choudhury and Fofana for parading the [[flag of Palestine]] during the post-match celebrations.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.independent.co.uk/sport/football/leicester-fa-cup-palestinian-flag-fofana-choudhury-b1848681.html|title=No punishment for Leicester's Palestinian flag celebrations at FA Cup final|work=[[The Independent]]|date=17 May 2021|access-date=18 May 2021|archive-date=17 May 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210517102812/https://www.independent.co.uk/sport/football/leicester-fa-cup-palestinian-flag-fofana-choudhury-b1848681.html|url-status=live}}</ref> This was despite it being claimed that such an action was against The FA's rules on political statements.<ref>{{Cite web |first=Sam |last=Cunningham |url=https://inews.co.uk/sport/football/hamza-choudhury-palestine-flag-fa-cup-final-leicester-rules-uefa-1005406 |title=Lack of action over Hamza Choudhury's Palestinian flag shows up football's contradictory rules about politics |publisher=I News |date=2021-05-18 |access-date=2021-05-24}}</ref>

The Leicester City [[Manager (association football)|manager]] [[Brendan Rodgers]] paid tribute to his side and the supporters: "I'm very proud, it's a historic day for the club. Winning the FA Cup for the first time is clearly a special day. The players were so courageous in the game{{nbsp}}... It was a fantastic atmosphere and I'm so happy Leicester supporters could be there to see us win it."<ref name=indyrep>{{Cite web | url = https://www.independent.co.uk/sport/football/brendan-rodgers-leicester-fa-cup-b1848211.html | work = [[The Independent]] | access-date = 22 May 2021 | title = Brendan Rodgers hails Leicester's courage after FA Cup final triumph | first = Nick | last = Mashiter | date = 16 May 2021 | archive-date = 15 May 2021 | archive-url = https://web.archive.org/web/20210515202639/https://www.independent.co.uk/sport/football/brendan-rodgers-leicester-fa-cup-b1848211.html | url-status = live }}</ref>  He described Tielemans' strike as "an old-school FA Cup-winning goal" but highlighted his goalkeeper's influence on the game, saying "{{nbsp}}... Kasper Schmeichel's saves – those are the special moments you need in games."<ref name=bbcreact/> It was Rodgers' seventh final win in seven attempts as a manager.<ref name=indyrep/> Schmeichel himself was jubilant: "To think of the people who have lifted this trophy, and to be able to do it today is beyond my wildest dreams."<ref name=bbcreact>{{Cite web | url = https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/57130809 | publisher = [[BBC Sport]] | access-date = 22 May 2021 | title = Leicester City: FA Cup-winning captain Kasper Schmeichel says joy 'indescribable' | date = 15 May 2021 | archive-date = 19 May 2021 | archive-url = https://web.archive.org/web/20210519192806/https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/57130809 | url-status = live }}</ref>  [[Thomas Tuchel]], the Chelsea manager, suggested that his team were "simply unlucky" and suggested that VAR had missed a handball in the build-up to the winning goal.<ref name=chelsreact>{{Cite web | url = https://www.chelseafc.com/en/news/2021/05/15/thomas-tuchel-reaction-to-chelsea-vs-leicester-in-the-fa-cup-fin | title = Tuchel labels Chelsea Cup Final performance unlucky and fives view on handball call | publisher = [[Chelsea F.C.]] | access-date = 22 May 2021 | date = 15 May 2021 | archive-date = 16 May 2021 | archive-url = https://web.archive.org/web/20210516181224/https://www.chelseafc.com/en/news/2021/05/15/thomas-tuchel-reaction-to-chelsea-vs-leicester-in-the-fa-cup-fin | url-status = live }}</ref>  He also described Tielemans' goal as "fantastic{{nbsp}}... but lucky".<ref name=chelsreact/>

Tielemans' goal was lauded in the media: the BBC described it as a "stunner",<ref>{{Cite web | url = https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/av/football/57129634 | publisher = [[BBC Sport]] | access-date = 21 May 2021 | title = FA Cup final: Youri Tielemans scores a stunner to give Leicester City the lead | date = 15 May 2021 | archive-date = 17 May 2021 | archive-url = https://web.archive.org/web/20210517170006/https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/av/football/57129634 | url-status = live }}</ref> Miguel Delaney of ''[[The Independent]]'' said that it was "one of the most spectacular FA Cup winners this competition will ever see",<ref>{{Cite web | url = https://www.independent.co.uk/sport/football/chelsea-leicester-result-score-fa-cup-final-b1848178.html | work = [[The Independent]] | access-date = 21 May 2021 | date = 16 May 2021 | first = Miguel | last = Delaney | title = Leicester win maiden FA Cup after Youri Tielemans' stunner sinks Chelsea | archive-date = 16 May 2021 | archive-url = https://web.archive.org/web/20210516095232/https://www.independent.co.uk/sport/football/chelsea-leicester-result-score-fa-cup-final-b1848178.html | url-status = live }}</ref> while David Hytner of ''[[The Observer]]'' called the goal a "firecracker" and one that "will live forever".<ref>{{Cite news | url = https://www.theguardian.com/football/2021/may/15/chelsea-leicester-city-fa-cup-final-match-report-youri-tielemans | work = [[The Observer]] | access-date = 21 May 2021 | first = David | last = Hytner | title = Leicester City win first FA Cup after Youri Tielemans screamer sinks Chelsea | date = 15 May 2021 | archive-date = 21 May 2021 | archive-url = https://web.archive.org/web/20210521080857/https://www.theguardian.com/football/2021/may/15/chelsea-leicester-city-fa-cup-final-match-report-youri-tielemans | url-status = live }}</ref>  It was declared "a remarkable goal, a thunderous strike" by [[CBS Sports]] and "a moment of magic" by Ali Humayun in ''[[The Athletic]]''.<ref>{{Cite web | url = https://www.cbssports.com/soccer/news/chelsea-vs-leicester-city-score-youri-tielemans-fires-foxes-to-their-first-fa-cup-win/live/ | work = [[CBS Sports]] | access-date = 21 May 2021 | date = 15 May 2021 | title = Chelsea vs. Leicester City score: Youri Tielemans fires Foxes to their first FA Cup win | first1 = James | last1 = Benge | first2 = Roger | last2 = Gonzalez | archive-date = 16 May 2021 | archive-url = https://web.archive.org/web/20210516065644/https://www.cbssports.com/soccer/news/chelsea-vs-leicester-city-score-youri-tielemans-fires-foxes-to-their-first-fa-cup-win/live/ | url-status = live }}</ref><ref>{{Cite web | url = https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/4212455/2021/05/15/leicester-win-fa-cup-after-beating-chelsea-1-0/ | work = [[The Athletic]] | access-date = 21 May 2021 | title = Leicester win FA Cup after beating Chelsea 1–0 | date = 15 May 2021 | url-access = subscription | first = Ali | last = Humayun | archive-date = 16 May 2021 | archive-url = https://web.archive.org/web/20210516152131/https://theathletic.com/news/fa-cup-final-chelsea-leicester-tielemans/Z0J3ex5bQnPd | url-status = live }}</ref>

As winners, Leicester City earned £1.8&nbsp;million in prize money, while runners-up Chelsea earned £900,000.<ref>{{cite web|date=28 April 2021|title=What time does the Emirates FA Cup Final kick-off and where can you watch it?|url=https://www.thefa.com/news/2021/apr/28/emirates-fa-cup-final-kick-off-confirmed-20210428|url-status=live|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210507150601/https://www.thefa.com/news/2021/apr/28/emirates-fa-cup-final-kick-off-confirmed-20210428|archive-date=7 May 2021|access-date=14 May 2021|publisher=[[The Football Association]]}}</ref> Leicester City also qualified for the [[2021–22 UEFA Europa League]] group stage.<ref>{{Cite web | url = https://www.skysports.com/football/news/11095/12276223/champions-league-europa-league-europa-conference-league-qualification-explained-who-will-be-playing-in-europe-next-season | publisher = [[Sky Sports]] | access-date = 21 May 2021 | title = Champions League, Europa League, Europa Conference League qualification explained: Who will be playing in Europe next season? | date = 20 May 2021 | archive-date = 20 May 2021 | archive-url = https://web.archive.org/web/20210520114305/https://www.skysports.com/football/news/11095/12276223/champions-league-europa-league-europa-conference-league-qualification-explained-who-will-be-playing-in-europe-next-season | url-status = live }}</ref> Furthermore, Leicester qualified for the [[2021 FA Community Shield]], where they beat [[2020–21 Premier League]] champions [[Manchester City F.C.|Manchester City]] 1–0.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Wilson |first1=Amie |title=Bertrand, Daka and Soumare outshine Man City's £100m man in Community Shield |url=https://www.leicestermercury.co.uk/sport/football/football-news/bertrand-daka-soumare-community-shield-5756717 |website=leicestermercury.co.uk|access-date=8 August 2021 |language=en |date=7 August 2021}}</ref> Chelsea became the first team since [[Newcastle United F.C.|Newcastle United]] in [[1998 FA Cup final|1998]] and [[1999 FA Cup final|1999]] to lose two consecutive FA Cup finals.<ref name=":0" />

